   "evidence": "`fourier_apply_add` (this file, line 29) gives `fourier n (x + -y) = fourier n x * fourier n (-y)`, and Mathlib `fourier_neg'` (mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/Fourier/AddCircle.lean:168, `toCircle (-(n \u2022 x)) = conj (fourier n x)`) gives `fourier n (-y) = conj (fourier n y)`. `hX.sub hY` is available: `ContinuousSub.measurableSub\u2082` (mathlib/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Constructions/BorelSpace/Basic.lean:611) applies since `AddCircle T` is a second-countable quotient group (mathlib/Mathlib/Topology/Algebra/Group/Quotient.lean:142) with the Borel structure already used by `measurable_add_const` in Basic.lean:228.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/Analysis/Fourier/AddCircle.lean",
   "fix": "Add `fourier_apply_sub (n : \u2124) (x y : AddCircle T) : fourier n (x - y) = fourier n x * conj (fourier n y)` next to `fourier_apply_add`, then define the pair lemma as `by simpa [fourier_apply_sub] using integrable_fourier_comp (hX.sub hY) n`, and use `fourier_apply_sub` to back the `e^{i n (\u03c6\u2c7c - \u03c6\u2096)}` claims in Basic.lean.",
   "issue": "`integrable_fourier_mul_conj_fourier` repeats the `Integrable.of_bound` argument of `integrable_fourier_comp` (line 36) for what is its `X - Y` instance: `fourier n x * conj (fourier n y) = fourier n (x - y)`. That identity is the general result here, is asserted three times in Basic.lean docstrings (lines 129, 148-149, 289-290: \"`e^{i n \u03c6\u2c7c} conj (e^{i n \u03c6\u2096}) = e^{i n (\u03c6\u2c7c - \u03c6\u2096)}`\"), and is never stated, so the public API carries an ad hoc two-variable, same-index, conj-shaped integrability lemma instead of the character lemma plus one integrability lemma.",
   "line": "43"
  }
 ],
